# Date and time display

Do not format user-facing dates or times with raw Carbon `->format()`, `strftime()`, or PHP `date()`.

Use the Afterburner core helper `format_date_superscript()` (ordinal superscript HTML). In packages, use `App\Support\TeamDateTime`:

- Team context: `\App\Support\TeamDateTime::formatDisplay($team, $dateTime, $includeTime)`
- Already-localized Carbon (e.g. calendar display timezone): `\App\Support\TeamDateTime::formatDisplayCarbon($carbon, $includeTime)`
- Calendar entry ranges: `\App\Support\TeamDateTime::formatCalendarEntrySchedule($startsAt, $endsAt, $allDay)`

Render HTML output with Blade unescaped syntax: `{!! $formatted !!}`.

Raw `->format()` is only for machine values: ISO dates, ICS exports, query strings, and form `wire:model` inputs.
